{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-meson-qcg-fusion-identity-mass-reading","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:meson-qcg-fusion-identity-mass-reading","kind":"remark","title":"The fusion identity and the meson mass-squared ratio","interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-meson-qcg-fusion-identity","tags":["meson","q-clebsch-gordan","interpretation"],"text":"meson-qcg-fusion-identity-mass-reading.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:meson-qcg-fusion-identity-mass-reading\"></a><p>The <a href=\"#prop:meson-qcg-fusion-identity\" data-at=\"braids-and-knots/lepton-meson-parallel\">fusion identity</a> is used as the categorical foundation for the meson mass-squared ratio <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m_K^2 / m_\\pi^2</code>. Since a meson is a 2-body state, its mass-squared is a bilinear quantity evaluated on the pair. The comparison of this ratio with measurement is made in <a href=\"#rem:meson-em-sinh-ratio-reading\" data-at=\"braids-and-knots/lepton-meson-parallel\">the meson ratio remark</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/meson-qcg-fusion-identity-mass-reading.md","heading":"Remark","number":"7.10.16","page":"b/rem-meson-qcg-fusion-identity-mass-reading"}
